„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter?¨sections—…¤book§chapter?«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄWho is this that cometh from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah? this that is glorious in his apparel, travelling in the greatness of his strength? I that speak in righteousness, mighty to save.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Wherefore art thou red in thine apparel, and thy garments like him that treadeth in the winefat?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter?«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙåI have trodden the winepress alone; and of the people there was none with me: for I will tread them in mine anger, and trample them in my fury; and their blood shall be sprinkled upon my garments, and I will stain all my raiment.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOFor the day of vengeance is in mine heart, and the year of my redeemed is come.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤And I looked, and there was none to help; and I wondered that there was none to uphold: therefore mine own arm brought salvation unto me; and my fury, it upheld me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And I will tread down the people in mine anger, and make them drunk in my fury, and I will bring down their strength to the earth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter?«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ%I will mention the lovingkindnesses of the LORD, and the praises of the LORD, according to all that the LORD hath bestowed on us, and the great goodness toward the house of Israel, which he hath bestowed on them according to his mercies, and according to the multitude of his lovingkindnesses.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\For he said, Surely they are my people, children that will not lie: so he was their Saviour.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹In all their affliction he was afflicted, and the angel of his presence saved them: in his love and in his pity he redeemed them; and he bare them, and carried them all the days of old.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter?«first_verse
