¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtBut they rebelled, and vexed his holy Spirit: therefore he was turned to be their enemy, and he fought against them.¦layout ªlast_verse
…¤book§chapter?«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃThen he remembered the days of old, Moses, and his people, saying, Where is he that brought them up out of the sea with the shepherd of his flock? where is he that put his holy Spirit within him?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„That led them by the right hand of Moses with his glorious arm, dividing the water before them, to make himself an everlasting name?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\That led them through the deep, as an horse in the wilderness, that they should not stumble?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘As a beast goeth down into the valley, the Spirit of the LORD caused him to rest: so didst thou lead thy people, to make thyself a glorious name.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter?«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉLook down from heaven, and behold from the habitation of thy holiness and of thy glory: where is thy zeal and thy strength, the sounding of thy bowels and of thy mercies toward me? are they restrained?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©Doubtless thou art our Father, though Abraham be ignorant of us, and Israel acknowledge us not: thou, O LORD, art our Father, our redeemer; thy name is from everlasting.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter?«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™O LORD, why hast thou made us to err from thy ways, and hardened our heart from thy fear? Return for thy servants' sake, the tribes of thine inheritance.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqThe people of thy holiness have possessed it but a little while: our adversaries have trodden down thy sanctuary.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQWe are thine: thou never barest rule over them; they were not called by thy name.¦layout ªlast_verse